From 5d4ddfa9df6ef857669acb4d554f91df8b673da2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabio <fabio@git.it>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:05:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] lib/http: stop server timeouts cutting off long uploads and
 downloads (backport)

--server-read-timeout and --server-write-timeout were applied from the
start of each request, so with the default of 1h any single upload or
download taking longer than an hour was cut off, for example a big file
over serve webdav, serve http or serve s3 on a slow link.

The timeouts now limit how long a transfer can go without progress: the
deadlines are pushed back each time some of the request body is read or
some of the response is written. A stalled transfer is still cut off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 lib/http/server.go              |  87 ++++++++++++++++++-
 lib/http/server_timeout_test.go | 147 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 231 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 lib/http/server_timeout_test.go

